---
source: crates/rumps-query/tests/scripts.rs
description: "; Test postfix operators on intrinsic expressions (@GET, @DATA, @ORDER, @QUERY)\n\n; Setup test data\n@SET d(1) = \"one\"\n@SET d(2) = \"two\"\n@SET d(3) = \"three\"\n\n; @GET with postfix ! (no parens needed)\n@OUTPUT @GET d(1)! AS String\n@OUTPUT @GET d(2)! AS String\n\n; @ORDER with postfix ! (returns Option[Subscript])\n@OUTPUT @ORDER d(0)!\n\n; @QUERY with postfix ! (returns Option[Array[Subscript]])\n@OUTPUT @QUERY d(0)!\n\n; Combined with other operations\nLET val = (@GET d(1)! AS String) ++ \" appended\"\n@OUTPUT val\n\n; Nested in expression context\n@OUTPUT ((@GET d(3)! AS String) ++ \" suffix\")\n\n; Works with subscript expressions too\nLET key = 2\n@OUTPUT @GET d(key)! AS String\n\n; Multiple postfix ops chained on @GET\n@SET arr(1) = 42\n@OUTPUT (@GET arr(1)! AS Int) + 8\n"
---
"one"
"two"
1
[ 1 ]
"one appended"
"three suffix"
"two"
50
